 ## Overview
-Mesh/Point Cloud Evaluation Metrics provides a comprehensive suite of geometric and topological measures to assess the fidelity and quality of reconstructed 3D surfaces against ground truth data [S2, S3, unofficial]. It addresses the problem of objectively quantifying reconstruction errors by combining point-wise proximity (Chamfer Distance), surface alignment (Normal Consistency), and threshold-based correctness (F-score), while also penalizing poor mesh topology (aspect ratios, self-intersections) [S2, S3, unofficial]. Unlike [Chamfer Distance](2446-chamfer-distance.md), which only measures average displacement, this method integrates precision/recall trade-offs and mesh regularity checks to provide a holistic quality assessment [S2, unofficial]. It differs from [Cloud-to-Mesh Accuracy Metrics](10560-cloud-to-mesh-accuracy-metrics.md) by evaluating symmetric point-cloud distances rather than orthogonal point-to-facet displacements [S1, S3, unofficial].
+Mesh/Point Cloud Evaluation Metrics provides a comprehensive suite of quantitative assessments for 3D surface and volumetric reconstructions, combining geometric accuracy (Chamfer Distance, F-score), normal consistency, and mesh topological quality (aspect ratios, self-intersections) [S2, S3, unofficial]. Unlike [Chamfer Distance](2446-chamfer-distance.md), which measures only point-wise proximity, this method evaluates geometric consistency under a distance threshold and penalizes irregular mesh structures [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from [Evaluation Pipeline](9358-evaluation-pipeline.md) by defining the specific mathematical functions for quality calculation rather than orchestrating the workflow, and from [Cloud-to-Mesh Accuracy Metrics](10560-cloud-to-mesh-accuracy-metrics.md) by including image-level metrics (PSNR) and volumetric mesh statistics [S1, S3, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The method evaluates a predicted mesh (or point cloud sampled from it) against a ground truth mesh by computing geometric accuracy, completeness, normal consistency, and topological regularity [S2, unofficial][S4].
+The method evaluates reconstructed geometry against ground truth data using point cloud sampling and mesh analysis. It computes accuracy, completeness, normal consistency, and F-score, alongside mesh quality indicators like aspect ratios and self-intersection counts [S2, unofficial][S4].
 
 ### Inputs and Outputs
